{
  "pedal": "Boss OC-5 Octave (mono: Input -> Output)",
  "comment": "Digital octaver; the GUITAR/BASS switch (top) on GUITAR throughout. Vintage = the OC-2's monophonic divider (-1 and -2 octaves) plus +1; Poly = polyphonic, -2 OCT/Range becomes Range (at its minimum only a chord's lowest note is shifted). Each octave is measured alone (Direct and the others fully down): its level law (-1 OCT, Direct), tone and waveform (a held 220 Hz sine), tracking (re-picked notes from 73 Hz to 1.3 kHz, 3 s apart: lowest and highest note, how fast it locks on), the fade (where the divider loses a dying note), chords (a low note under a higher one) and Range; then the guitar DI (captures/di/phrases.wav) at six blends for a by-ear A/B. Clock positions: 7:00 = fully counter-clockwise, 5:00 = fully clockwise; 9:00 and 3:00 pointer horizontal.",
  "knobs": [
    "Mode",
    "Direct Level",
    "+1 OCT Level",
    "-1 OCT Level",
    "-2 OCT/Range"
  ],
